    "created_at": "2019-05-29T03:08:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-29T03:08:19Z",
    "body": "> the [`autocomplete=one-time-code`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#attr-fe-autocomplete-one-time-code) specification doesn't tell a website author enough to know how they should send an SMS that'll actually autofill on the user's platform\r\n\r\nFWIW, SMS isn't the only delivery mechanism for one-time passwords so I don't think defining how to use SMS to autofill the value should be a requirement for this specification. For example, some password managers have built-in TOTP clients that could fill their value into the field. Having the hint that a field is for a one-time-code makes this much easier for agents helping the user compared to `autocomplete=off` (especially on `<input type=password>` where that `off` values is often ignored nowadays).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
