    "created_at": "2020-04-29T15:16:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-29T15:18:25Z",
    "body": "My day job utilizes OTP as first-factor authentication, whether or not that's a good idea isn't up for discussion :)\r\n\r\nFor the sake of others in the same position I'd recommend having wording in the specification that implementations of input fields with the `autocomplete=one-time-code` property (especially in tandem with `type=password`) ensure that baked-in password managers don't ask the user if they wish to save the password - a foolish endeavor.\r\n\r\nAs all major browsers ignore `autocomplete=off` on password inputs at the moment of writing - our workaround has been use of the `type=text` input with a custom security-circle font, as `text-security` CSS isn't adopted outside of webkit.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
